{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-253887",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Given a random variable $X∼Exp(\\lambda ),$ and two positive real numbers $s,t,$ the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =2,$ $s=1,$ and $s+t=3.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt=(t+s)-s=3-1=2\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>3\\,|\\,X>1) & ={e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & ={e}^{-(1/2)\\cdot (2)} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
